WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.813
There are four basic relational terms that are
useful to translate into

00:00:03.826 --> 00:00:09.560
everyday language A relation is essentially a table
about one subject

00:00:09.587 --> 00:00:14.471
or event type A tuple is one row in that table An

00:00:14.497 --> 00:00:19.247
attribute is a column that describes each row A
domain describes the

00:00:19.273 --> 00:00:24.733
allowed type and rules for a value For example the
patient table

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.933
is the relation One patient is a tuple Birth date is
an

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:34.328
attribute The allowed type and constraints on birth
date are part of

00:00:34.354 --> 00:00:40.282
its domain One important word is atomic Atomic

00:00:40.308 --> 00:00:45.150
does not mean physically small It means the database
treats the field

00:00:45.176 --> 00:00:50.679
as one value If a column contains a comma-separated
list of service

00:00:50.705 --> 00:00:54.692
codes and each service needs to be searched joined
or validated separately

00:00:54.863 --> 00:00:57.995
that list is not a good atomic design for the
relational model
